# BLoC Patterns — Bardak

## Events & States

Events and states MUST be `sealed` classes extending `Equatable`:

```dart
// ✅ events
sealed class WordPacksEvent extends Equatable {
  const WordPacksEvent();
}
class LoadWordPacks extends WordPacksEvent {
  const LoadWordPacks({required this.locale});
  final String locale;
  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [locale];
}

// ✅ states
sealed class WordPacksState extends Equatable {
  const WordPacksState();
}
class WordPacksLoaded extends WordPacksState {
  const WordPacksLoaded({required this.packs, required this.locale});
  final List<WordPackEntity> packs;
  final String locale;
  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [packs, locale];
}
```

## Concurrency Transformers

Every async `on<Event>` handler MUST declare an explicit transformer.
No silent default (concurrent) processing for user-triggered actions.

```dart
import 'package:bloc_concurrency/bloc_concurrency.dart';

on<RefreshPacks>(_onRefresh, transformer: restartable());   // search / refresh
on<SubmitTap>(_onSubmit, transformer: droppable());         // one-shot tap
on<SaveSettings>(_onSave, transformer: sequential());       // order matters
```

Omit only for initialization events where concurrent is intentional — add a comment.

## Bloc vs Cubit

- Use **Bloc** when events are discrete user actions or external triggers.
- Use **Cubit** only for simple state machines driven by method calls
  (e.g., `RewardsCubit` exposing `addCoins()`, `openBox()`).

## Constructor Injection

BLoCs receive UseCases via constructor parameters. Never call `getIt()` inside a BLoC.

```dart
// ✅
class SettingsBloc extends Bloc<SettingsEvent, SettingsState> {
  SettingsBloc({
    required this.getGameSettingsUseCase,
    required this.updateAppSettingsUseCase,
  }) : super(...) { ... }

  final GetGameSettingsUseCase getGameSettingsUseCase;
  final UpdateAppSettingsUseCase updateAppSettingsUseCase;
}

// ❌ Never
class SettingsBloc extends Bloc<SettingsEvent, SettingsState> {
  SettingsBloc() : _uc = getIt<GetGameSettingsUseCase>(), super(...);
}
```

## File Layout

Co-locate event, state, and bloc in `presentation/bloc/`:
```
feature/presentation/bloc/
  feature_event.dart
  feature_state.dart
  feature_bloc.dart
```

## Logging

Use `AppBlocObserver` (already wired in `main.dart`). Log via `log()` from `dart:developer`.
Never use `print()` or `debugPrint()` in BLoC or observer code.
